SUMMARY

A semiconductor is a material that can conduct electricity under some conditions but not others. It is used to control electrical current in devices like computers and phones.

📖 Explanation  
- Semiconductors have electrical properties between conductors (like metals) and insulators (like rubber).  
- Their ability to conduct electricity can be changed by adding impurities (called doping).  
- Common semiconductor materials include silicon and germanium.  
- They are the foundation of modern electronics, used in transistors, diodes, and integrated circuits.  
- Semiconductors help control the flow of electricity, making devices smaller, faster, and more efficient.

==================================================

